  "id": "k-complex",
  "term": "K complex",
  "definition": "A K complex is a prominent EEG waveform seen during the second stage of non-REM sleep. It is a biphasic slow wave that stands out from the background brain activity and may occur on its own or be triggered by external stimuli.",
